.TH WINLUXCD 1 "August 2026" "WinLuxCD 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
winluxcd \- convert Windows (PowerShell) directory addresses to WSL cd commands
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B winluxcd
.RI [ \-p | \-w | \-c ]
.RI [ PATH ]
.br
.B winluxcd
.B \-h
.br
.B winluxcd
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B winluxcd
converts a Windows path such as
.B C:\eUsers\eyou\eDocuments
into a WSL path such as
.BR /mnt/c/Users/you/Documents ,
and prints it as a
.B cd
command you can paste straight into a WSL terminal.
.PP
When called without
.IR PATH ,
.B winluxcd
reads the current Windows clipboard
(via
.BR powershell.exe\ Get-Clipboard )
and converts that.
.PP
Windows paths may use backslashes or forward slashes and may be wrapped in
single or double quotes.  Paths that are already in WSL form are passed through
unchanged.  UNC paths such as
.B \\\\server\eshare
are rendered as
.BR //server/share .
.PP
The converter uses
.BR wslpath (1)
when available and falls back to a built-in converter otherwise.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-p
Print just the converted path, without the
.B cd
prefix.
.TP
.B \-w
Reverse direction: convert a WSL path to a Windows path.
.TP
.B \-c
Convert and copy the resulting
.B cd
command to the Windows clipboard.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show usage information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version number and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.TP
.B winluxcd 'C:\eUsers\eyou\eDocuments'
cd "/mnt/c/Users/you/Documents"
.TP
.B winluxcd
Convert whatever is currently on the Windows clipboard.
.TP
.B winluxcd -p 'D:/work/Project X'
/mnt/d/work/Project X
.TP
.B winluxcd -w /home/you
C:\eUsers\eyou  (or \\\\wsl.localhost\\e... on some setups)
.TP
.B cd "$(winluxcd -p)"
Jump to the converted directory in the current shell.
.SH SHELL INTEGRATION
The installer adds a
.B winluxcd
function to
.B ~/.bash_aliases
which changes the current directory:
.RS
.PP
winluxcd 'C:\eUsers\eyou\eDocuments'   \fI# jumps into /mnt/c/Users/you/Documents\fP
.br
winluxcd                                  \fI# jumps to the clipboard path\fP
.RE
.PP
Flags such as
.B \-p,
.B \-w
and
.B \-c
are passed through to the
.B winluxcd
script unchanged.
.SH POWERSHELL
A PowerShell twin lives in the project at
.BR powershell/winluxcd.ps1 .
It accepts the same ideas: convert, \fI\-Windows\fP for the reverse direction,
\fI\-Clipboard\fP, \fI\-Copy\fP and \fI\-Raw\fP.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.local/bin/winluxcd
Installed executable (main script).
.TP
.B ~/.bash_aliases
Sourced by the stock Ubuntu .bashrc; holds the cd function.
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/icons/...
Installed icon files (PNG, SVG and a Windows ICO).
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/applications/winluxcd.desktop
Optional launcher shown in WSLg/desktop app menus.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wslpath (1)
.SH AUTHOR
The WinLuxCD project.
